{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>With your mouth</b> — to instruct you what you shall speak to Pharaoh. For now He did not say that Aaron would speak on his behalf, but only to the people, as it is stated, <b>and he shall speak, he, to you, to the people</b>; but to Pharaoh, Moses himself would speak — and perhaps this was for the dignity of the kingship. But in the end Moses returned and said, \"Behold, I am of uncircumcised lips, and how will Pharaoh listen to me?\" (Exodus 6:30), and He gave him permission not to speak even to Pharaoh — and this is a distinction for Moses. Therefore He said there, \"See, I have made you Elohim to Pharaoh, and Aaron your brother shall be your prophet\" (Exodus 7:1). And the sense of <b>and with his mouth</b> is that the words of his mouth would find favor with those who hear."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:02:32.651149095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}